{
 "about": "Field classes of the mechanisms domain (VERIFY_HARDENING 6.3, lint L-WATCH; WP-D mechanisms; docs/domains/mechanisms.md section 21). 'fields' classifies, for this domain's types (house_sim/data/types/mechanisms.json), every property of the type data the kernel's name table does not and every field this domain's verbs and systems write: identity = what the hardware is (latch and handle kinds, ratings, panels' buttons, a pump's stroke, a closer's delay); setting = a configuration the robot sets (panels, lift and tilt, hasps, child stops, pump head and nozzle, modes, lock points; a rod's and a track's word: a repair changes them too, the damage itself is on the record's damage map; open_frac, lift_frac and tilt_deg with the tolerance of a hand's setting); condition = damage in its worse direction (jammed, strain, bent slats, torn hooks, cross-threaded, what a sprayer put on a thing); process = a mirror or consequence of a setting, judged at the setting (bolt_throw follows locked; gap_cm, coverage, privacy_ok follow the panels and the lift; clear_opening_m2 and egress_ready follow the sash; closers' and rain's running values; a touchscreen's page); bookkeeping = records of what happened (mech.kind is written on first use and always equals what the type infers; timers' due times, test records, press and flush counters, damage notes, what was spilled: the spill itself is a mess parcel). 'types': the ledger applies 'fields' only to a domain's own types, and most closures this domain works are the kernel's (door, gate, window, drawer, ...): FOR_CORE_TYPES of mech.* are repeated per type for the kernel's closure types and other domains' with a mechanism kind (request to WP1: read 'writes'; then these per-type copies can go). 'water_sensitive': this domain's electronics (house.wet). 'writes': the names of 'fields' this domain writes on things of ANY type.",
